messages:
ella: Heads-up — I'm opening a docs PR to add a 'tier mapping' sample pack for migrations from the old slab tiers to the new global tiers. Need eyeballs on the examples and the dashboard panel link.

sam: Thanks — can you paste the snippet you plan to add? I want to sanity-check the header names and the example responses.

ella: Pasting a minimal SDK example I was going to include (js). It's intended to show the header we set for per-request tier selection and the recommended fallback.

ella: ```js
// choose-tier.js
const resp = await client.generate({
  model: 'redwood-llama-3',
  input: 'Summarize the release notes',
  headers: {
    'x-redwood-tier': 'team-provisioned:gold', // prefer this tier
    'x-redwood-fallback': 'auto-cost', // allow fallback to cheaper variant
  }
});
console.log(resp.output);
```

matt: Looks good. Two small asks: (1) show example when the header is absent (i.e., default mapping), and (2) call out that the header is case-insensitive in the API (we sometimes forget to mention that).

jia: Also we should add a tiny JSON example of the meter labels returned in usage analytics so customers can wire their dashboards. Something like:

jia: ```json
{
  "meters": [
    {"name":"tokens","tier":"gold","amount":12345},
    {"name":"requests","tier":"gold","amount":37}
  ]
}
```

ella: Good call. I'll add both. One important edge case: burst credits from legacy slabs convert to a temporary 'graceAllowance' object during migration. We should document how that shows up in the quota API and the dashboard panel (panel id changed from panel_legacy_quota to panel_quota_v2).

sam: Can we include the exact query URL for the dashboard panel? PM asked for a direct link they can paste into onboarding emails.

ella: Sure — internal link (infra only): https://console.redwood.ai/dashboard/panel_quota_v2?team={{team_id}}. I'll include the templated link and call out it requires the new doc-perm role to view.

matt: Tiny editorial nit: avoid calling the new tiers "slab" anywhere in the new doc — that term is legacy and causes confusion in support tickets.

ella: noted. I'll replace slab -> legacy-slab where historical context is needed.

docs-bot: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4821 — reviewers: @sam @matt @jia

sam: I'll review today; if we need a small rephrase for the billing team I'll ping finance.

jia: I'll add the meter label example to the analytics reference page too and link back to the migration guide.

ella: Thanks all. I'll push the updated examples in the next commit and ping once CI passes. :thumbsup:
